  "updated_at": "2026-10-19T15:00:02Z",
  "body": "In fact, option A—augmented with a union type rather than replacing the type with a function—is the better choice. The proposed version A would require you to provide a function every single time, even when you only need to specify a static value; while that might not seem like much extra typing, it would almost certainly become quite tiresome sooner or later.",
